<section class="section faq-section" id="faq">
    <div class="reveal" style="text-align:center;">
        <div class="section-tag" style="margin:0 auto 20px;"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question" aria-hidden="true"></i> FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Common Questions</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin:0 auto;">Everything you need to know about SchoolSync.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
            <div class="faq-question">
                How long does it take to set up SchoolSync for my school?
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Most schools are up and running within 30 minutes. Simply register your school, add your classes, and start adding students. Our auto-generate feature creates everything based on your school type — Pre-Primary to KG-12.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
            <div class="faq-question">
                Can I use SchoolSync for Gujarati or Hindi medium schools?
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Absolutely! SchoolSync is built specifically for Indian schools. We support Gujarati, Hindi, and English mediums. The interface works seamlessly in all languages, and you can switch anytime from the language selector.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
            <div class="faq-question">
                Is my school's data secure?
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes, security is our top priority. We use bank-grade encryption (256-bit SSL), regular automated backups, and role-based access control. Your data is stored on secure Indian servers and never shared with third parties.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
            <div class="faq-question">
                Can I import existing student data from Excel?
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes! We provide a simple Excel template. Just fill in your student data and upload it. Our system automatically validates and imports everything — names, classes, parent details, and more.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
            <div class="faq-question">
                What happens after the 7-day free demo?
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>After your 7-day free demo, you can choose any of our plans — Basic (₹999/month), Standard (₹2,499/month), or Premium (₹4,999/month). No hidden fees, no setup charges. You can upgrade, downgrade, or cancel anytime.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
            <div class="faq-question">
                Do you provide training for teachers and staff?
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes! We offer free video tutorials, documentation, and live webinars. Premium plan users get dedicated onboarding support and 1-on-1 training sessions for their staff.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item reveal">
            <div class="faq-question">
                Who can use the In-App Chat feature?
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Chat access is role-based and controlled by the school admin. Admins can enable or restrict chat permissions for teachers, students, and parents individually. Group chats and direct messages are available on Standard plan and above, ensuring safe and monitored communication within the school.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
